# UI Core

## Components

- Prefer small and reusable components
- Prefer composition over prop-heavy abstractions
- Keep business logic outside UI components
- Avoid giant screens and components

## Layout

- Prefer responsive and flexible layouts
- Avoid hardcoded dimensions when possible
- Ensure layouts support small screens and font scaling

## Safe Area

- Respect safe area insets on all screens
- Avoid content behind status and navigation bars
- Prefer `react-native-safe-area-context`

## Interaction

- Prefer `Pressable` for interactive elements
- Provide visual feedback for interactions
- Ensure accessible touch targets

## Inputs and Keyboard

- Prevent keyboard overlap on inputs and forms
- Keep focused inputs visible while typing
- Handle keyboard behavior consistently across platforms
- Prefer keyboard-aware layouts when necessary

## Accessibility

- Prefer semantic and accessible components
- Support screen readers and dynamic font sizes
- Avoid interaction-only communication

## Performance

- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Avoid expensive calculations inside components
- Prefer memoization only when necessary
